3. No AI or machine-learning training

Unless the applicable copyright holder grants you separate written
permission, you may not use Covered Material, in whole or in part, as input,
training data, labels, targets, rewards, exemplars, or other learning material
for training, pre-training, continued training, fine-tuning, reinforcement
learning, distillation or other fitting or updating of the learned weights
or parameters of any artificial-intelligence or machine-learning model,
including language models, code models and large language models.

You may not collect, scrape, convert, annotate, synthesize or distribute
Covered Material, or data generated from it that reproduces or reconstructs
its protectable expression, for those purposes. In particular, changing its
format, translating it, generating code explanations or question/answer
pairs from it, or routing it through another model does not remove this
restriction when the resulting material contains such expression.

You may not authorize a third party to perform these prohibited activities
under this license. When you send Covered Material to a model service for a
permitted purpose, use a service and configuration whose applicable terms do
not permit that submission to be used for the prohibited training purposes.

4. Permitted intelligent assistance and language capabilities

Section 3 does not prohibit inference with an already trained model to
explain, search, review, debug, complete, modify or generate programs or
documentation; retrieval-augmented assistance; creating or searching an
embedding index using fixed model weights; executing agents; robot/device
control; or the language's self-inspection and self-modification features.
These uses are permitted provided they do not fit or update model weights
or learned parameters from Covered Material or supply it for Section 3's
prohibited purposes. Editing ordinary code, prompts, workflows, configuration
or explicit task memory is not itself model training under this license.

Using the language or runtime solely as a tool to train a model on your own
independent data is also permitted, provided Covered Material is not used as
learning material. This license places no restriction on independently
created outputs merely because Chaos was used to produce them; any Covered
Material reproduced in an output remains subject to this license.

